  "evidence": "The check 'assert_orders_fresh' attached to stg_orders failed (1 row) because there are orders with order_date older than 30 days. Querying staging.stg_orders shows many rows with order_date well before CURRENT_DATE - 30 days (e.g., 1996-01-02, 1993-10-14, etc.). The raw source table raw.orders contains these historic dates (COUNT = 14957 rows, max date 1998-07-27). The test expects zero rows older than 30 days, indicating the source data now includes older records that were not expected. This is a data issue at the source, not a code issue. Therefore the incident is caused by upstream data and should be escalated to the source owner."
}
